{:edb/db-before-t 2248 :edb/db-after-t 2249 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535561 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:31:57.326Z" 13194139535561 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355206 13194139535561 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355213 13194139535561 true] [17592186179662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355220 13194139535561 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355192 13194139535561 true] [17592186179663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186355199 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1017 #edb/ref 17592186355193 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1089 "q-124181" 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1100 "If ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=8$ and ${\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$ given that $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1113 #uuid "0bc49a3e-94e5-5e0b-b0a0-e39ca31b0568" 13194139535561 true] [17592186355192 1145 "Let $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ be a piecewise smooth path in the $xy$-plane, and let $-C$ be the curve consisting of the same points as $C$ but with the opposite orientation. \n\nFor line integrals with respect to $y,$ we have the following properties:\n\n- ${\\int }_{-C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=-{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-8-(-3) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535561 true] [17592186355193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355194 13194139535561 true] [17592186355193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355195 13194139535561 true] [17592186355193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355196 13194139535561 true] [17592186355193 1000 #edb/ref 17592186355197 13194139535561 true] [17592